The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established [[Gamers8]] series. '''Rocket League''' was announced to be part of the EWC line-up for the next 3 years on December 12, 2025.<ref name="EWC RL">{{cite web|url=https://www.linkedin.com/posts/esports-world-cup-foundation_ewc2026-esportsworldcup-fortnite-activity-7407089025892712448-LcXW|title=Fortnite and Rocket League have joined the lineup of competitive titles for the Esports World Cup 2026, as part of an exciting new three-year partnership with Epic Games.|date=2025-12-17|publisher=[[Esports World Cup Foundation]]|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} English}}</ref> It was originally planned to be hosted in Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, but was moved to Paris, France on May 20.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/2057121960623006162|title=Esports World Cup 2026 is coming to Paris|author=Esports World Cup|author-link=Esports World Cup|date=2026-05-20}}</ref>

:''See [[esports:Esports World Cup/2026|here]] to read about the Esports World Cup 2026, the Calendar, the Club Standings and more.''

==About==
===Format===
*'''Group Stage''' - ''August 12th - 14th, 2026''
**16 teams split into 2 GSL Groups of 8.
*** Upper Bracket matches are {{Bo|5}}
*** Lower Bracket matches are {{Bo|7}}.
*<span class="mw-customtoggle-nation-ranking1" style="border-bottom:1px dotted;">''Group Stage Seeding Rules:''</span>
<div class="table-responsive">
<div class="toccolours mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" id="mw-customcollapsible-nation-ranking1" style="width:760px; margin-left:45px">
** Teams are split into 4 seed pools to ensure balanced groups.
*** 16 teams are split into 4 pools:
**** '''Pool 1''' will consist of RLCS Europe Ranking #1 and RLCS Middle East & North Africa Ranking #1.
**** '''Pool 2''' will consist of RLCS Europe Ranking #2 and RLCS North America Ranking #1.
**** '''Pool 3''' will consist of RLCS Europe Ranking #3, RLCS Middle East & North Africa Ranking #2, RLCS Middle East & North Africa Ranking #3, RLCS North America Ranking #2, RLCS North America Ranking #3, RLCS South America Ranking #1, RLCS South America Ranking #2, and the EWC Title Defender.
**** '''Pool 4''' will consist of RLCS Asia Pacific Ranking #1, RLCS Oceania Ranking #1, RLCS Sub-Saharan Africa Ranking #1, and EWC Last Chance Qualifier #1.
** If the EWC Title Defender earns a different qualifier seed, they will receive the higher starting seed, and the RLCS Europe Ranking #4 team will inherit the EWC Title Defender seed.
** Teams will be drawn into groups by random selection.
*** For the purposes of the draw, the EWC Title Defender is considered part of Europe.
** Each group will feature one team from Pool 1, one team from Pool 2, four teams from Pool 3, and two teams from Pool 4.
** Each region may only represent a maximum of 50% of the teams in a group, rounded up.
** If a team is drawn into a group where they would be ineligible, they will be assigned to the other group in the drawing order instead.
</div></div>
**Top 4 Teams per group - 8 in total - advance to the [[#Playoffs|Playoffs]].
*'''Playoffs''' - ''August 15th - 16th, 2026''
**Single Elimination Bracket.
***Upper Bracket Teams will be drawn randomly against a Lower Bracket Team. Teams from the same Group can not play against each other.
***All matches ''(excl. 3rd Place)'' are {{Bo|7}}.
**** 3rd Place match is a {{Bo|5}}.

